# Decimal remainder with double operands

Takes 10.5 modulo 2.25 in both operand orders to verify the f64 value
converts into a decimal remainder, producing 1.50 when the decimal is the
dividend and 1.5 when the double is the dividend.

>>> source
decimal_value: decimal = 10.5
double_divisor: double = 2.25
double_dividend: double = 10.5
decimal_divisor: decimal = 3

// Verifies the Decimal/Double conversion.
decimal_remainder: decimal = decimal_value % double_divisor
print(decimal_remainder)

// Verifies the same conversion with the operand order reversed.
double_remainder: decimal = double_dividend % decimal_divisor
print(double_remainder)

<<< stdout
1.50
1.5

<<< stderr
